@title Course Scheduling Frontend
@subtitle Choosing a framework for the admin app rewrite, Internal Tools guild, Wrenfield University IT
@author Internal Tools guild

The course-scheduling admin app has about 60 screens, mostly forms and tables, and 5 developers will rewrite it.

# Criteria

- Team familiarity
- Form and table libraries
- Hiring pool
- Bundle size
- Long-term support

# Comparison

table = Framework,Team familiarity,Form/table ecosystem,Bundle size (KB),Hiring pool; React,4 of 5 developers,excellent,142,large; Vue,1 of 5 developers,good,98,medium; Svelte,0 of 5 developers,fair,41,small

# Pros and cons

### React
- Pro: 4 of 5 developers already know it.
- Pro: the data grid we need exists today.
- Con: largest bundle at 142 KB.

### Vue
- Pro: good form and table ecosystem.
- Pro: smaller bundle at 98 KB.
- Con: only 1 developer knows it.

### Svelte
- Pro: smallest bundle at 41 KB.
- Pro: favorite in the prototype spike.
- Con: no one on the team knows it.
- Con: small hiring pool and a fair ecosystem.

# Recommendation

! Choose **React**, mainly because four of the five developers already know it and the data grid we need exists today.

> We are optimizing for the next five years of maintenance, not the first five weeks of building.
> — Hannah Osei, guild lead

Svelte was the favorite in the prototype spike, and we will revisit it for smaller tools.
